ADVANCED EXCEL NOTES

1. IF FUNCTION

IF function ka use kisi condition ko check karne ke liye kiya jata hai.

Syntax:
=IF(condition, value_if_true, value_if_false)

Example:
=IF(B2>=40,"Pass","Fail")

Agar marks 40 ya usse zyada hain to Pass aayega, otherwise Fail.

---

2. AND FUNCTION

AND function ka use multiple conditions ko check karne ke liye hota hai. Isme sabhi conditions TRUE honi chahiye.

Syntax:
=AND(condition1, condition2, ...)

Example:
=IF(AND(B2>=40,C2>=40),"Pass","Fail")

---

3. OR FUNCTION

OR function ka use multiple conditions mein se kisi ek condition ke TRUE hone par kiya jata hai.

Syntax:
=OR(condition1, condition2, ...)

Example:
=IF(OR(B2>=40,C2>=40),"Pass","Fail")

---

4. SUMIF FUNCTION

SUMIF function kisi particular condition ke according values ka total calculate karta hai.

Syntax:
=SUMIF(range, criteria, sum_range)

Example:
=SUMIF(A2:A10,"Lucknow",B2:B10)

Is formula se Lucknow ki total sales calculate hongi.

---

5. SUMIFS FUNCTION

SUMIFS function multiple conditions ke according total calculate karta hai.

Syntax:
=SUMIFS(sum_range, criteria_range1, criteria1, criteria_range2, criteria2)

Example:
=SUMIFS(C2:C10,A2:A10,"Lucknow",B2:B10,"Laptop")

Ye Lucknow mein Laptop ki total sales calculate karega.

---

6. COUNTIF FUNCTION

COUNTIF kisi particular condition ko satisfy karne wale cells ki counting karta hai.

Syntax:
=COUNTIF(range, criteria)

Example:
=COUNTIF(B2:B20,">=50")

Ye 50 ya usse zyada marks wale students ko count karega.

---

7. COUNTIFS FUNCTION

COUNTIFS multiple conditions ke according cells ko count karta hai.

Syntax:
=COUNTIFS(range1, criteria1, range2, criteria2)

Example:
=COUNTIFS(B2:B20,">=50",C2:C20,"Pass")

---

8. AVERAGEIF FUNCTION

AVERAGEIF kisi condition ke according average calculate karta hai.

Syntax:
=AVERAGEIF(range, criteria, average_range)

Example:
=AVERAGEIF(A2:A10,"Delhi",B2:B10)

Ye Delhi ki average sales calculate karega.

---

9. VLOOKUP

VLOOKUP ka use table ke first column mein kisi value ko search karke usi row se required information nikalne ke liye hota hai.

Syntax:
=VLOOKUP(lookup_value, table_array, col_index_num, FALSE)

Example:
=VLOOKUP(E2,A2:D10,3,FALSE)

E2 mein di hui value ko A2:D10 table mein search karega aur third column ki value return karega.

---

10. XLOOKUP

XLOOKUP ek modern lookup function hai. Iska use kisi value ko search karke corresponding result find karne ke liye hota hai.

Syntax:
=XLOOKUP(lookup_value, lookup_array, return_array)

Example:
=XLOOKUP(E2,A2:A10,C2:C10)

---

11. INDEX AND MATCH

INDEX aur MATCH ko combine karke advanced lookup kiya ja sakta hai.

MATCH kisi value ki position find karta hai aur INDEX us position ki value return karta hai.

Formula:
=INDEX(C2:C10,MATCH(E2,A2:A10,0))

---

12. IFERROR

IFERROR ka use formula mein error aane par custom message show karne ke liye hota hai.

Syntax:
=IFERROR(formula, value_if_error)

Example:
=IFERROR(VLOOKUP(E2,A2:C10,3,FALSE),"Not Found")

Agar value nahi milti hai to "Not Found" show hoga.

---

13. CONDITIONAL FORMATTING

Conditional Formatting ka use kisi condition ke according cells ko automatically highlight karne ke liye hota hai.

Examples:
• 40 se kam marks ko highlight karna.
• Top 10 values highlight karna.
• Duplicate values highlight karna.
• Data Bars lagana.
• Color Scales use karna.

Path:
Home → Conditional Formatting

---

14. DATA VALIDATION

Data Validation ka use Excel mein data entry ko control karne ke liye hota hai.

Example:
Gender column mein sirf Male, Female aur Other allow karna.

Path:
Data → Data Validation

Iska use dropdown list banane ke liye bhi kiya jata hai.

---

15. PIVOT TABLE

Pivot Table ek powerful Excel tool hai jo large amount of data ko summarize aur analyze karne ke liye use hota hai.

Pivot Table se hum:
• Total Sales
• Average Sales
• Region-wise Sales
• Product-wise Sales
• Month-wise Sales

calculate kar sakte hain.

Main sections:
• Rows
• Columns
• Values
• Filters

Path:
Insert → PivotTable

---

16. SLICER

Slicer Pivot Table ko interactive filter banata hai.

Example:
Region ke liye Lucknow, Delhi, Mumbai jaise buttons bana sakte hain.

User kisi region par click karke sirf us region ka data dekh sakta hai.

Path:
PivotTable Analyze → Insert Slicer

---

17. PIVOT CHART

Pivot Chart Pivot Table ke data ka graphical representation hota hai.

Common Pivot Charts:
• Column Chart
• Bar Chart
• Line Chart
• Pie Chart

Pivot Chart ka use dashboards aur reports mein hota hai.

---

18. POWER QUERY

Power Query Excel ka data cleaning aur transformation tool hai.

Power Query ka use:
• Data import karne ke liye
• Duplicate remove karne ke liye
• Blank values handle karne ke liye
• Columns split karne ke liye
• Columns merge karne ke liye
• Data type change karne ke liye
• Multiple files combine karne ke liye
• Tables merge karne ke liye

Path:
Data → Get & Transform Data

---

19. WHAT-IF ANALYSIS

What-If Analysis ka use different situations ke results ko analyze karne ke liye hota hai.

Main tools:

1. Goal Seek
2. Scenario Manager
3. Data Table

---

20. GOAL SEEK

Goal Seek ka use required result achieve karne ke liye input value find karne mein hota hai.

Example:
Agar required profit ₹50,000 hai to Goal Seek calculate kar sakta hai ki required sales kitni honi chahiye.

Path:
Data → What-If Analysis → Goal Seek

---

21. EXCEL DASHBOARD

Excel Dashboard ek interactive visual report hota hai jo important information ko ek hi screen par show karta hai.

Dashboard mein generally:
• KPI Cards
• Charts
• Pivot Tables
• Slicers
• Filters
• Sales Summary

use kiye jate hain.

Example:
SALES DASHBOARD

Total Sales
Total Orders
Average Sales
Top Product
Region-wise Sales
Monthly Sales
Sales Trend

---

22. MACROS

Macro ka use repetitive tasks ko automatically perform karne ke liye hota hai.

Macro ko record karke same task ko baar-baar automatically perform karwa sakte hain.

Path:
View → Macros → Record Macro

Advanced automation ke liye VBA (Visual Basic for Applications) ka use kiya jata hai.

---

